trek73 for OS-9/68000=====================ORIG holds comp.sources.games volume 3, Trek73 4.0 (six parts), as posted.The files beside it build the OS-9 program.  grammar.c in ORIG is theposters' own yacc output and is not built: y.tab.c and lex.yy.c here weremade on OS-9 from grammar.y and command.l with the disk's yacc and flex.What changed, and why:  every file  Each source opens with #ident, which Microware's cpp rejects              even inside a skipped #if, so each is a comment here.  defines.h   SIGALRM is 5 under OSK, the signal unix.l's alarm() sends;              signal.h does not name it.  main.c      stdin->_cnt = 0 empties stdio's buffer on Unix; Microware's  save.c      FILE has no _cnt, and stdin->_ptr = stdin->_end does the same.              buffering() leaves stdio's own choice under OSK instead of              testing fstat() for a character device.  Before each command              is parsed, yyrestart() gives flex a fresh start.  save.c      A game is saved by writing the whole data segment, from              `version' to sbrk(0), and restored with brk(); OS-9 does not              lay a program's memory out that way, so under OSK saving and              restoring each say they are not possible.  The save-file              directory is $HOME, with no password-file fallback.  parsit.c    The turn timer's alarm interrupts the read of a command.  On              OS-9 that leaves stdin in error and unix.l runs the signal              handler only at check_signal(), so every later read failed at              once and turns ran on without waiting.  Under OSK Gets()              empties the line, clears stdin and calls check_signal().  subs.c      Microware's math library has atan() and no atan2(); a small              atan2() built on atan() is used.  command.l   flex defines input() and unput() itself, so the lex versions              at the end are left out and flex reads the command through              YY_INPUT.  Input and Inptr are defined in globals.c, so they              are extern here: l68 takes a second definition as a clash.getopt.c and the other sources build unchanged apart from their #identlines.  printships, shipyard and bpv are not built.Build: cc cmds1.c cmds2.c cmds3.c cmds4.c damage.c dist.c endgame.c          enemycom.c firing.c globals.c init.c main.c misc.c mission.c          moveships.c parseopts.c save.c ships.c special.c strat1.c subs.c          vers.c parsit.c getopt.c y.tab.c -DOSK -DSYSV -DPARSER -l=math.l